* Wed Sep 30 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.1.0-1
- Reap the daemon's own "(Waydroid)" profiles when Android no longer has the
  SSID saved. Until now a network forgotten in Android left its profile, PSK
  included, in NetworkManager forever: NmBackend::forget() implements exactly
  this and nothing called it (docs/59).
- The supplicant seam cannot carry that signal, and this was measured before
  anything was built. ISupplicantStaIface.removeNetwork fires on every
  reconnect, not on a forget -- four times in one boot on a network that was
  never forgotten and was still connected -- so calling forget() there would
  have deleted the profile the host is administered over every time Wi-Fi was
  used.
- Ownership is tested by the daemon's deterministic RFC 4122 v5 UUID over a
  fixed namespace and the SSID, not by the " (Waydroid)" label, which the
  desktop GUI can rename and NM does not require to be unique. This also
  corrects two pre-existing name-based ownership tests in this script, which
  were sparing host profiles from a deletion their owner had opted into and
  handing renamed projections to the wrong half of the script.
- The reap runs BEFORE the allow-list gate, because an empty allow-list is the
  default and our projections exist regardless; the host-owned half is still
  opt-in and still exits early. The allow-list is parsed first so nodelete can
  protect an SSID in both halves.
- Guarded five ways: our UUID, absent from Android, never active on a device,
  never autoconnect=yes, and never more than MAX_REAPS_PER_RUN (1) at once. The
  last gets its own budget rather than sharing MAX_FORGETS_PER_RUN because once
  Android has lost a passphrase our profile holds the last copy of it.

* Sat Sep 26 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First package. The credential reconciler and its timer, split out of
  waydroid-wifid.spec's `sync` subpackage so a fix to a shell script on a timer
  no longer reissues the C++ daemon (docs/47).
- Installs through the `wifi-sync` component of artifacts/wifi/install.sh, which
  is what lets that installer serve one modification at a time.
- Ships /etc/waydroid-wifi-share.conf at 0600 with no network named in it, as
  %%config(noreplace): until an SSID is written into it this package copies
  nothing anywhere (docs/36).
